<http://dbpedia.org/resource/USS_Bold_(BAT-8)> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "single Fairbanks Morse Main Reduction GearShip's Service Generatorsone Diesel-drive 60 kW 120 V D.C.one Diesel-drive 30 kW 120 V D.C.**USS *Bold* (BAT-8),** was a Favourite class [tugboat](:Tugboat) built for the [British](:United_Kingdom) along the lines of American ATR-1-class rescue tugs. She was transferred to the [United Kingdom](:United_Kingdom) on 29 June 1942 and was operated as **HMS *Bold* (W114)** by the [Royal Navy](:Royal_Navy).She was returned to the [United States Navy](:United_States_Navy) at [Subic Bay](:Subic_Bay) in the [Philippines](:Philippines) in January 1946. *Bold* was struck from the [Navy List](:Naval_Vessel_Register) on 17 July 1947. On 29 June 1948, she was sold to Bosey, [Philippines](:Philippines), though never delivered. On 2 October 1948, Bosey resold her to T. Y. Fong."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
