<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Ningbo> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "[29°51′37″N 121°37′28″E﻿ / ﻿29.8603°N 121.6245°E﻿ / 29.8603; 121.6245](https://geohack.toolforge.org/geohack.php?pagename=Ningbo&params=29.8603_N_121.6245_E_type:adm2nd_region:CN-33_source:Gaode)**Ningbo** ([simplified Chinese](:Simplified_Chinese_characters): 宁波; [traditional Chinese](:Traditional_Chinese_characters): 寧波; [pinyin](:Pinyin): *Níngbō*; [Ningbonese](:Ningbo_dialect): [*gnin² poq⁷*](:Romanization_of_Wu_Chinese) Template:IPA-wuu, [Standard Mandarin](:Putonghua) pronunciation:  ), [formerly romanized](:Chinese_postal_romanization) as **Ningpo**, is a major [sub-provincial city](:Sub-provincial_city) in northeast [Zhejiang](:Zhejiang) [province](:Provinces_of_China), [People's Republic of China](:China). It comprises 6 urban districts, 2 [satellite county-level cities](:County-level_city), and 2 rural counties, including several islands in [Hangzhou Bay](:Hangzhou_Bay) and the [East China Sea](:East_China_Sea). Ningbo is the southern economic center of the [Yangtze Delta megalopolis](:Yangtze_Delta), and is also the core city and center of the [Ningbo Metropolitan Area](:Ningbo_Metropolitan_Area). To the north, [Hangzhou Bay](:Hangzhou_Bay) separates Ningbo from [Shanghai](:Shanghai); to the east lies [Zhoushan](:Zhoushan) in the [East China Sea](:East_China_Sea); on the west and south, Ningbo borders [Shaoxing](:Shaoxing) and [Taizhou](:Taizhou%2C_Zhejiang) respectively. As of the [2020 Chinese National Census](:Seventh_National_Population_Census_of_the_People%27s_Republic_of_China), the entire administrated area of Ningbo City had a population of 9.4 million (9,404,283), of which 4,479,635 lived in the built-up (or metro) area of its five urban districts. Within the next decade, the cities of Cixi, Yunhao and Fenghua will likely also be [conurbated](:Conurbation), expanding the Ningbo metro area to 8,140,660 inhabitants.Ningbo is one of the 15 [sub-provincial cities](:Sub-provincial_city) in China, and is one of the 5 [separate state-planning cities](https://zh.wikipedia.org/wiki/计划单列市) in China (the other four being [Dalian](:Dalian), [Qingdao](:Qingdao), [Xiamen](:Xiamen), and [Shenzhen](:Shenzhen%29), with the municipality possessing a separate state-planning status in many economic departments, rather than being governed by [Zhejiang Province](:Zhejiang). Therefore, Ningbo has provincial-level autonomy in making economic and financial policies.In 2020, the [GDP](:Gross_domestic_product) of Ningbo was CNY 1240.87 billion (US$191.68 billion), and it was ranked 12th among 300 cities in China. Moreover, Ningbo is among the wealthiest cities in China; it ranked 8th in terms of average yearly disposable income in the year of 2020. As of 2020, Ningbo has global headquarters and registered offices of over 100 listed companies, and many regional business headquarters. In 2021, Ningbo featured the 7th most listed companies of all cities in China. Furthermore, Ningbo was among the top 10 Chinese cities in the Urban Business Environment Report released by the Chinese state media [China Central Television (CCTV)](:CCTV-1) in 2019.As a city with rich culture and a long history dating back to the [Jingtou Mountain Culture](https://zh.wikipedia.org/wiki/井头山遗址) in 6300 BC and the [Hemudu culture](:Hemudu_culture) in 4800 BC, Ningbo was awarded \"City of Culture in East Asia\" by the governments of China, Japan, and Korea in 2016. Ningbo is one of the top 200 cities in the world by scientific research as tracked by the [Nature Index](:Nature_Index).The [port of Ningbo–Zhoushan](:Port_of_Ningbo%E2%80%93Zhoushan), spread across several locations, is the world's [busiest port by cargo tonnage](:List_of_busiest_ports_by_cargo_tonnage) and world's third-[busiest container port](:List_of_busiest_container_ports) since 2010."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
