<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Groupe_Latécoère> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The **Groupe Latécoère** (Template:IPA-fr is an aircraft company based in [Toulouse](:Toulouse), France. Founded by the [aeronautics](:Aerospace) pioneer [Pierre-Georges Latécoère](:Pierre-Georges_Lat%C3%A9co%C3%A8re) during 1917, the company became well known in its first few decades for its range of [seaplanes](:Seaplane), such as the six-engined [Latécoère 631](:Lat%C3%A9co%C3%A8re_631).Presently, Groupe Latécoère operates as a major supplier of aerostructures, producing sections of fuselage and doors, having become the second-largest European supplier of onboard [electrical wire harnesses](:Cable_harness) and [avionics](:Avionics) bays through its *Latelec* [subsidiary](:Subsidiary) company. It is currently a member of the [CAC Small](:CAC_Small) and participates in all segments of aeronautics: commercial [airliners](:Airliner) with [Airbus](:Airbus) and [Boeing](:Boeing), [regional aircraft](:Regional_aircraft) with [Embraer](:Embraer) and [Bombardier](:Bombardier_Aerospace), [business aircraft](:Business_aircraft) with [Dassault Aviation](:Dassault_Aviation), as well as military aircraft with Dassault and Airbus."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
