<http://dbpedia.org/resource/La_Victoria,_Aragua> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "La Victoria (Spanish pronunciation: [la βikˈtoɾja]) is a city in the state of Aragua in Venezuela. It is famous for the independence battle of 12 February 1814, the Battle of La Victoria, where José Félix Ribas led a young and inexperienced army that succeeded in halting the royalist troops of José Tomás Boves at La Victoria. Venezuela celebrates \"Youth Day\" every 12 February in La Victoria, with a ceremony usually presided over by the President of the Republic."@en .
