<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Doncaster_Works> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Doncaster Railway Works is a railway workshop located in Doncaster, England. Also referred to as 'The Plant\", it was established by the Great Northern Railway in 1853, replacing the previous works in Boston and Peterborough. Until 1867 it undertook only repairs and maintenance. Today the remaining part is operated by Wabtec."@en .
