<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Nissan_Sentra> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The **Nissan Sentra** is a series of automobiles manufactured by the [Japanese](:Japan) automaker [Nissan](:Nissan) since 1982. Since 1999, the Sentra has been categorized as a [compact car](:Compact_car), while previously it occupied the [subcompact](:Subcompact_car) class. Until 2006, Sentra was a rebadged export version of the Japanese [Nissan Sunny](:Nissan_Sunny), but since the 2013 model year, Sentra is a rebadged export version of the [Sylphy](:Nissan_Sylphy). The Sentra nameplate is not used in Japan. Many other countries in Latin America sell their versions of the Sunny as the Sentra. In Mexico, the first three generations of the Sentra were known as the **Nissan Tsuru** (Japanese for [crane](:Red-crowned_crane%29), and the B13 model was sold under that name until 2017, alongside the updated models badged as Sentra.In North America, the Sentra currently serves as Nissan's compact car, despite being rated as a [mid-size car](:Mid-size_car) by the [EPA](:EPA) due to its interior volume since the 2007 model year. While previous Sentras were subcompacts, the Sentra has grown over the years, with the [Nissan Versa](:Nissan_Versa) having replaced the Sentra in the entry-level area.The Sentra name was created for Nissan by Ira Bachrach of [NameLab](:NameLab), and Bachrach describes the origin as \"Nissan wanted consumers to understand that it was quite safe even though it was small. The word Sentra sounds like central as well as sentry, which evokes images of safety.\""^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
