<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Chevrolet_Camaro_(fourth_generation)> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The **fourth-generation [Chevrolet Camaro](:Chevrolet_Camaro)** is a [pony car](:Pony_car) that was produced by American automobile manufacturer [General Motors](:General_Motors) for the 1993 through 2002 model years. It was introduced on an updated [F-body platform](:GM_F_platform), but retained the same characteristic since the first-generation's introduction back in 1967; 2-doors, 2+2 seating, [coupé](:Coup%C3%A9) (with optional [T-top](:T-top) roof) or [convertible](:Convertible_%28car%29) bodystyles, [rear-wheel drive](:Automobile_layout), and a choice of [OHV](:Overhead_valve_engine) [V6](:V6_engine) and [V8](:V8_engine) engines. The Camaro was revised in 1998 with both exterior and engine changes. [General Motors](:General_Motors) discontinued production of the fourth generation of the Camaro due to slow sales, a deteriorated sports coupé market, and plant overcapacity."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
