<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Supercharger> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "In an internal combustion engine, a supercharger compresses the intake gas, forcing more air into the engine in order to produce more power for a given displacement. The current categorisation is that a supercharger is a form of forced induction that is mechanically powered (usually by a belt from the engine's crankshaft), as opposed to a turbocharger, which is powered by the kinetic energy of the exhaust gasses. However, up until the mid-20th century, a turbocharger was called a \"turbosupercharger\" and was considered a type of supercharger."@en .
