<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Fiat_E.torQ_engine> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The E.torQ is a family of inline-4 gasoline automobile engines produced since 2011 by Fiat Chrysler Automobiles in Campo Largo, Brazil in the former Tritec factory. The E.torQ series is an update on the Tritec engine, albeit re-engineered by Fiat Powertrain Technologies with an investment of €83 million. Updates include a high pressure injected aluminum block from the previous iron, and upgraded motors and controllers for the CNC machines used in the manufacturing process to increase productivity and ease diagnosis. The engine block has cylinder head fittings separate from the cylinder jackets, the threads are positioned in the upper part of the water jackets, and the connections between the jackets and the outside are kept apart from the cylinder head fittings. 80% of torque becomes avail"@en .
