<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Willamette_Iron_and_Steel_Works> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Willamette Iron Works (also known as Willamette Iron and Steel Company or WISCO) was a general foundry and machine business established in 1865 in Portland, Oregon, originally specializing in the manufacture of steamboat boilers and engines. In 1904, the company changed its name to Willamette Iron and Steel Works, under which name it operated continually until its close in 1990. In the early 1970s, the company manufactured the first three turbine units for the third powerhouse to be built at Grand Coulee Dam. The company also made fire hydrants for the city of Portland in the late 19th century."@en .
