<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Chevrolet_Camaro_(third_generation)> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The third-generation Chevrolet Camaro is an American pony car which was introduced for the 1982 model year by Chevrolet. It continued to use General Motors' F-body platform and produced a \"20th Anniversary Commemorative Edition\" for 1987 and \"25th Anniversary Heritage Edition\" for 1992. These were also the first Camaros with factory fuel injection, four-speed automatic transmissions, five-speed manual transmissions, four-cylinder engines, 16-inch wheels, and hatchback bodies. For 1987 a convertible Camaro was reintroduced, converted by ASC in relatively small numbers. The third-generation Camaro continued through the 1992 model year."@en .
