<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Bombardier_Transportation> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "**Bombardier Transportation** was a Canadian-German [rolling stock](:Rolling_stock) and [rail transport](:Rail_transport) manufacturer, headquartered in [Berlin](:Berlin), Germany.It was one of the world's largest companies in the rail vehicle and equipment manufacturing and servicing industry. Bombardier Transportation had many regional offices, production and development facilities worldwide. It produced a wide range of products including [passenger rail vehicles](:Passenger_car_%28rail%29), [locomotives](:Locomotive), [bogies](:Bogie), [propulsion](:Ground_propulsion) and controls. In February 2020, the company had 36,000 employees, and 63 manufacturing and engineering locations around the world.Formerly a subsidiary and [rail](:Rail_transport) equipment division of [Bombardier Inc.](:Bombardier_Inc%2E), the company was acquired by French manufacturer [Alstom](:Alstom) on 29 January 2021."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
