<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Suzuki_TS50X> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The **Suzuki TS50X** is an [air-cooled](:Air-cooled_engine), 49 cc (3.0 cu in), [single-cylinder](:Single-cylinder_engine), [two-stroke](:Two-stroke) engined, [trial](:Types_of_motorcycles%23Off-road) style [motorcycle](:Motorcycle) manufactured by [Suzuki](:Suzuki) from 1984 to 2000. It had a five-speed [manual](:Manual_transmission) gearbox and complied with the United Kingdom requirements of the time to be classified as a moped. Electrics were 12 volt and [capacitor discharge](:Capacitor_discharge_ignition) electronic ignition was used.The machine used Suzuki's own *CCI* oil pump delivery system, avoiding the need to pre-mix two-stroke engine oil.The [duplex cradle](:Motorcycle_frame) type frame, is made of welded tubular steel with a steel box-section [swingarm](:Swingarm). Front suspension is conventional coil-sprung [telescopic](:Telescopic_fork), but the rear has Suzuki's [\"full-floater\"](:Suspension_%28motorcycle)#Mono-shock) type where the suspension is connected to the frame by a linkage, which allows spring rates to increase in response to wheel travel."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
