<http://dbpedia.org/resource/HMS_Lark_(1762)> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "HMS Lark was a 32-gun Richmond-class frigate fifth-rate frigate of the Royal Navy. She was launched in 1762 and destroyed in Narragansett Bay in 1778, during the American Revolutionary War. Between 29 May and 18 July, the British captured a number of vessels: the sloops Sally and Fancy, snow Baron D'Ozell,Olive Branch, sloop Betsey, and schooner Sally. Lark shared the prize money with Kingfisher, , , and the Pigot galley. The remains of Lark are now part of a site listed on the National Register of Historic Places, the \"Wreck Sites of HMS Cerberus and HMS Lark.\""@en .
