<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Serco_Marine_Services> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "**Serco Marine Services** is a [Private Finance Initiative](:Private_Finance_Initiative) contract, with [Serco Group](:Serco), to deliver auxiliary services to [His Majesty's Naval Service](:His_Majesty%27s_Naval_Service) (incl. [Royal Navy](:Royal_Navy), [Royal Marines](:Royal_Marines) and [Royal Fleet Auxiliary](:Royal_Fleet_Auxiliary%29).Marine Services primarily operates from the nation's three main naval bases, [HMNB Portsmouth](:HMNB_Portsmouth), [HMNB Devonport](:HMNB_Devonport) and [HMNB Clyde](:HMNB_Clyde), but also supports training and operations overseas, as well as at various [British Overseas Territories](:British_Overseas_Territories).Serco Denholm (a joint venture between Serco Group and [Denholm Group](:Denholm_Group%29)won the Marine Services contract, replacing the subsequently disbanded [Royal Maritime Auxiliary Service](:Royal_Maritime_Auxiliary_Service). Denholm's participation was bought out in late 2009 by its larger partner, Serco."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
