<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Zhengzhou> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "**Zhengzhou** (; [simplified Chinese](:Simplified_Chinese_characters): [郑州](https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/郑州); [traditional Chinese](:Traditional_Chinese_characters): [鄭州](https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/鄭州); [pinyin](:Pinyin): *Zhèngzhōu*), also spelt **Zheng Zhou** and [alternatively romanized](:Chinese_postal_romanization) as **Chengchow**, is the [capital](:Capital_%28political%29) and largest city of [Henan Province](:Henan) in the [central part](:Central_China) of the [People's Republic of China](:China). Located in north-central Henan, it is one of the [National Central Cities](:National_Central_City) in China, the centre of [Central Plains](:Central_Plain_%28China%29) area, and serves as the political, economic, technological, and educational center of the province. The Zhengzhou metropolitan area (including Zhengzhou and [Kaifeng](:Kaifeng%29) is the core area of the [Central Plains Economic Zone](:Central_Plains_Economic_Zone).The city lies on the southern bank of the [Yellow River](:Yellow_River). Zhengzhou is a major hub of China's national transportation network, with railways connecting Zhengzhou to Europe and an international airport. Zhengzhou is a National Civilized City [[zh](https://zh.wikipedia.org/wiki/全国文明城市)] and a [State-list Famous Historical and Culture City](:List_of_National_Famous_Historical_and_Cultural_Cities_in_China). As of 2020, there are two [World Cultural Heritage Sites](:List_of_World_Heritage_Sites_in_China) in Zhengzhou. The [Zhengzhou Commodity Exchange](:Zhengzhou_Commodity_Exchange) (ZCE) is China's first futures exchange. [Zhengzhou Airport Economy Zone](:Zhengzhou_Airport_Economy_Zone) is China's first Airport Economy Zone.As of the [2020 Chinese census](:2020_Chinese_census), the [prefecture-level city](:Prefecture-level_city) of Zhengzhou had a population of 12,600,574 inhabitants, whom 10,260,667 lived in its built-up (or metro) area made of 6 urban districts plus Zhongmu county, Xinzheng and Xingyang cities now largely being conurbated. The city had a total GDP of 1.014 trillion (RMB) in 2018. Greater Zhengzhou was named as one of the 13 emerging mega-cities in China in a July 2012 report by the [Economist Intelligence Unit](:Economist_Intelligence_Unit), and officially named as the eighth National Central City in 2017 by the central government in Beijing.Zhengzhou is a major city for scientific research, appearing among the world's top 100 [cities](:List_of_cities_by_scientific_output) as tracked by the [Nature Index](:Nature_Index). The city is home to [several national key universities](:List_of_universities_and_colleges_in_Henan) in China, notably [Zhengzhou University](:Zhengzhou_University), [Henan University](:Henan_University), [Henan Agricultural University](:Henan_Agricultural_University), [Henan University of Chinese Medicine](:Henan_University_of_Chinese_Medicine), and [Henan University of Technology](:Henan_University_of_Technology)."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
