<http://dbpedia.org/resource/EMD_SD28> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "An **EMD SD28** is a 6-axle diesel [locomotive](:Locomotive) built by [General Motors Electro-Motive Division](:Electro-Motive_Diesel) between July 1965 and September 1965. Power was provided by an [EMD 567D1](:EMD_567D1) 16-[cylinder](:Cylinder_%28engine%29) engine which generated 1,800 horsepower (1.34 MW). This locomotive was basically a non-turbocharged version of the [EMD SD35](:EMD_SD35). 6 examples of this locomotive model were built for [American](:United_States) railroads.A passenger variant, type SDP28, was built for export to Korea in May 1966, with 6 delivered. Only 1 SD28 is left it is owned by Cargill and operates in Iowa."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
