<http://dbpedia.org/resource/San_Pedro,_Los_Angeles> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "San Pedro (/sænˈpiːdroʊ/, san-PEE-droh; Spanish \"St. Peter\") is a neighborhood within the City of Los Angeles, California. Formerly a separate city, it consolidated with Los Angeles in 1909. The Port of Los Angeles, a major international seaport, is partially located within San Pedro. The district has grown from being dominated by the fishing industry, to a working-class community within the city of Los Angeles, to a rapidly gentrifying community."@en .
