<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Brattvåg> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Brattvåg is a village in Ålesund Municipality in Møre og Romsdal county, Norway. The village is located on the Norwegian mainland, along the west side of the . It is located about 12.5 kilometres (7.8 mi) northwest of the villages of Vatne/Eidsvik. The 1.74-square-kilometre (430-acre) village has a population (2018) of 2,426 and a population density of 1,394 inhabitants per square kilometre (3,610/sq mi). The newspaper Nordre is published in Brattvåg. Prior to 2020, it was the administrative centre of the old Haram Municipality."@en .
