<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Overhead_camshaft_engine> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "An overhead camshaft (OHC) engine is a piston engine where the camshaft is located in the cylinder head above the combustion chamber. This contrasts with earlier overhead valve engines (OHV), where the camshaft is located below the combustion chamber in the engine block."@en .
