<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Deutsche_Werke> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "**Deutsche Werke** was a German [shipbuilding](:Shipbuilding) company that was founded in 1925 when [Kaiserliche Werft Kiel](:Kaiserliche_Werft_Kiel) and other shipyards were merged. It came as a result of the [Treaty of Versailles](:Treaty_of_Versailles) after [World War I](:World_War_I) that forced the German defense industry to shrink. The company was owned by the government of the [Weimar Republic](:Weimar_Republic) and its headquarters was in [Berlin](:Berlin) while the manufacturing location was in [Kiel](:Kiel).Deutsche Werke started building [merchant ships](:Merchant_ship), but when the [Nazi Party](:Nazi_Party) gained power in 1933 the production was changed to [naval ships](:Naval_ship). Besides shipbuilding, Deutsche Werke also produced [firearms](:Firearm). Especially well-known are the so-called [Ortgies](:Ortgies_7%2E65_mm_Semi-Automatic_Pistol) [pistols](:Pistol), which were particularly popular in the [United States](:United_States). The pistols were developed by Heinrich Ortgies.During World War II the company expanded to [Gdynia](:Gdynia), establishing *Deutsche Werke Gotenhafen*.Deutsche Werke facilities and infrastructure were destroyed during [World War II](:World_War_II) by [bombing raids](:Bombing_raid). Parts of the works were reorganised as [Maschinenbau Kiel](:Maschinenbau_Kiel).In 1955 the shipyard areas were bought by [Howaldtswerke](:Howaldtswerke-Deutsche_Werft)."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
