<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Nissan_X-Trail> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The **Nissan X-Trail** ([Japanese](:Japanese_language): 日産・エクストレイル, [Hepburn](:Hepburn_romanization): *Nissan Ekusutoreiru*) is a [compact crossover SUV](:Compact_crossover_SUV) produced by the Japanese automaker [Nissan](:Nissan) since 2000. Since its introduction, the X-Trail is positioned below the truck-based [Xterra](:Nissan_Xterra) and [Pathfinder](:Nissan_Pathfinder).Since the third-generation model, the X-Trail became the same vehicle as the North American market [Rogue](:Nissan_Rogue). For the first time, the X-Trail became available with three-row seating as an option. It also marked a departure in terms of design from a rugged boxy look to an urban-oriented crossover SUV design. The fourth-generation model introduced an e-Power [series hybrid](:Series_hybrid) powertrain option, which became the sole option in Japan and Europe.As of 2022[[update]](//en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Nissan_X-Trail&action=edit), the X-Trail is positioned between the smaller [Qashqai](:Nissan_Qashqai) – which the X-Trail shares platform with – and the larger [Pathfinder](:Nissan_Pathfinder) in Nissan's global crossover SUV line-up."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
