<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Corvette> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A corvette is a small warship. It is traditionally the smallest class of vessel considered to be a proper (or \"rated\") warship. The warship class above the corvette is that of the frigate, while the class below was historically that of the sloop-of-war. The modern types of ships below a corvette are coastal patrol craft, missile boat and fast attack craft. In modern terms, a corvette is typically between 500 tons and 2,000 tons, although recent designs may approach 3,000 tons, which might instead be considered a small frigate."@en .
