<http://dbpedia.org/resource/USS_Ossipee_(1861)> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The first USS Ossipee was a wooden, screw sloop-of-war in commission in the United States Navy at various times between 1861 and 1889. She served in the Union Navy during the American Civil War. She was named for the Ossipee River of New Hampshire and Maine. The USS Ossipee was present during the Alaska Purchase."@en .
